  "notes": "USAGE: {捏|こ}ねる is an ichidan verb used primarily in cooking and crafting contexts.\n\nTRANSITIVITY: Transitive (takes を)\n\nASPECT: {捏|こ}ねている indicates ongoing kneading action or habitual kneading.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n・{生地|きじ}を{捏|こ}ねる (to knead dough)\n・{粘土|ねんど}を{捏|こ}ねる (to knead clay)\n・{理屈|りくつ}を{捏|こ}ねる (to quibble, make excuses)\n・{屁理屈|へりくつ}を{捏|こ}ねる (to nitpick, make sophistic arguments)\n\nKANJI NOTE: The kanji {捏|こ}ねる uses a relatively uncommon character. Often written in hiragana as こねる in casual contexts.\n\nRELATED:\n・{練|ね}る - to knead, to train, to refine\n・{混|ま}ぜる - to mix",
